From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:01:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 177/307] feat: LPV stability overhaul - dedicated RSM, stable
 propagation, debug views

Major stability work on the resurrected Light Propagation Volumes:

- Dedicated sun RSM view (e_LPVRsm frustum, r_LPVDedicatedRSM): fitted to
  the LPV volume, camera orientation independent caster collection via
  volume overlap membership instead of traversal marking, fixed traversal
  bit, well conditioned virtual light distance.
- Gather-only propagation with explicit running sum (CE3 scheme), replacing
  the compounding variant that amplified checkerboard modes.
- Temporal accumulation with integer cell reprojection, relight gating
  (heartbeat r_LPVUpdateInterval), SVOGI style cell albedo secondary bounce.
- Fix D3D11 SRV hazard: the deferred decal pass leaves scene normals bound
  as render target, silently nulling the apply pass SRV whenever a decal is
  visible - the screen space apply now runs after ShadowMask (LPV APPLY),
  right before the tiled shading combine.
- Fix pre-existing engine bugs: 64-bit frustum mask wiped by 32-bit BIT()
  in UpdateCullMask; cascade swallow loop consuming unrelated cached passes.
- Debug suite r_LPVDebug 1-11: CPU state logs, per-object cull/submission
  tracing, staged injection probes, surface mosaic, instanced probe spheres.
- Full case file of the display flicker investigation in
  investigations/gi_lpv/07_flicker_case_file.md.

